  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "• Preheat oven to 220°C/200°C fan-forced.\n• Cut sweet potato into small chunks.\n• Cut brown onion into wedges.\n• Spread veggies over a lined oven tray. Drizzle with olive oil, season with salt and pepper and toss to coat. Roast until tender, 20-25 minutes. TIP: If your oven tray is crowded, divide the veggies across two trays!",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/recipe/step-67595b63daedc2bd1295a580-1ea3e73a.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Meanwhile, finely chop garlic.\n• Drain and rinse white rice.\n• In a medium saucepan, melt the butter with a dash of olive oil over medium heat. Cook half the garlic until fragrant, 1-2 minutes.\n• Add rice, the water (for the rice) and a generous pinch of salt. Stir, then bring to the boil. Reduce heat to low and cover with a lid. Cook for 10 minutes, then remove from heat. Keep covered until rice is tender and water is absorbed, 10 minutes. TIP: The rice will finish cooking in its own steam, so don’t peek!",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/recipe/step-67595b63daedc2bd1295a580-7505f7cc.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• While the rice is cooking, drain sweetcorn.\n• Drain and rinse chickpeas.\n• Finely chop cucumber.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/recipe/step-67595b63daedc2bd1295a580-f67a34d5.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Heat a large frying pan over high heat. Cook sweetcorn until lightly charred, 4-5 minutes. Transfer to a medium bowl.\n• To the bowl with corn, add cucumber and a drizzle of white wine vinegar and olive oil. Toss to combine. Season, then set aside. TIP: Cover the pan with a lid if the corn kernels are “popping” out.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/recipe/step-67595b63daedc2bd1295a580-66c9b541.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• SPICY! The spice blend is mild, but use less if you're sensitive to heat. Return the frying pan to medium heat with a drizzle of olive oil. Cook tomato paste, chickpeas, Tex-Mex spice blend (see ingredients) and the remaining garlic, tossing, until fragrant, 1-2 minutes.\n• Add the water (for the sauce) and vegetable stock pot. Bring to a simmer and cook until tender, 3-4 minutes (if the mixture looks too thick, add a splash more water).\n• Remove from heat. Lightly crush chickpeas. Stir through roasted veggies. Season to taste.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/recipe/step-67595b63daedc2bd1295a580-606c2b77.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Divide garlic rice between bowls.\n• Top with chickpeas, light sour cream and tomato salsa.\n• Sprinkle with Cheddar cheese.\n• Tear over coriander to serve. Enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/recipe/step-67595b63daedc2bd1295a580-18adb0f9.jpeg"
    }
  ]
}
